==============================================================================
Scope of the MIT License
==============================================================================

The MIT License above covers only the original work written for this project:

  - the TypeScript/TSX source code under `src/` (including `src/game/ccb`,
    `src/game/atlas`, `src/game/world`, `src/game/screens`, `src/game/session`,
    `src/game/locale`, `src/game/network` and `src/game/boot.ts`) and the
    files `src/App.tsx`, `src/main.tsx`, `src/index.css`;
  - the mock server under `mock-server/` (its game data is invented);
  - the analysis scripts under `tools/` and the text of the documents written
    by the author (`README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/*.md`);
  - the build and configuration files at the repository root.

Everything listed in the next section is NOT covered by the MIT License.


==============================================================================
Legal notice: material that is not MIT licensed
==============================================================================

1. This is an unofficial, fan-made, non-commercial project. It is NOT
   affiliated with, authorized, sponsored or endorsed by Social Point, its
   owners or licensors, or by anyone who publishes Dragon City. "Dragon City",
   "Social Point" and every related name, logo and character are trademarks or
   copyrighted works of their respective owners.

2. Game assets. The contents of `src/assets/` were copied unchanged from the
   `assets/` folder of the official Dragon City 2.0 Android APK (11 May 2013):
   images, user-interface files (`.ccbi`), fonts, sounds, shaders, animations,
   masks, texts and localization tables. They are the property of their
   respective owners, are NOT licensed under the MIT License, and no license
   to them is granted by this repository. They are included only so the
   project can run for study and preservation purposes. If you redistribute or
   fork this repository, you are responsible for deciding whether you may
   include them; the safe course is to remove `src/assets/` and use your own
   lawfully obtained copy of the game.

3. Data recovered from the game binary. `docs/re-output/` holds raw dumps
   (symbol names, strings, command and key lists, the label colour table)
   produced by analysing `libdc.so` from that APK. They are derived from
   third-party software and are NOT licensed under the MIT License. A few
   facts recovered the same way are embedded in the source for interoperability
   (for example the response-signing key, the label colour table in
   `src/game/ccb/palette.ts`, file formats, layout constants and message
   formats). The author claims no ownership of them and they are used solely to
   make an independent implementation compatible with the original.

4. Code derived from the Flash client. Code that was ported from, or derived
   from, the decompiled Flash client of the game (for example the number
   formatter in `src/game/core/format.ts` and the older Flash-era code in
   `src/game/core`, `src/game/engine`, `src/game/renderer` and
   `GamePlayer.tsx`) is NOT covered by the MIT License. The decompiled client,
   the original APK, `libdc.so` and the original servers are not part of this
   repository and must not be added to it.

5. Dependencies. Third-party packages (Pixi.js, pixi-viewport, React, Vite and
   others) keep their own licenses, found in their packages.

6. Purpose. The author does not intend to make any profit from this project:
   it is not sold, has no advertising, no payments and no monetization, and it
   is offered free of charge for learning, research, interoperability and
   game preservation. It does not connect to the original game servers by
   default; it talks to the mock server included here, whose data is invented.
   Nobody may use this project to impersonate the original game or its
   publisher.

7. No warranty and takedown. The project is provided "as is", with no warranty
   of any kind (see the MIT License above). This notice is not legal advice. If
   you are a rights holder and believe any material here should not be
   distributed, open an issue or contact the maintainer and it will be removed
   promptly.
